From 5a193a4ce9aeed21a3e4de2e72c60300433ee211 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fi3 <you@example.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 08:57:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ADD strict backend slash-command routing for
 selected-agent chat

Route slash-prefixed selected-agent chat through the provider command hook so backend commands do not enter the normal prompt path. The default backend implementation returns an unsupported-command reply, while Codex uses the app-server command action for existing sessions.
---
 docs/architecture.md              |  12 ++-
 src/agent_runtime.rs              |  14 ++-
 src/cli.rs                        | 140 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/codex.rs                      |  97 ++++++++++++---------
 tests/agent_core.rs               |   4 +-
 tests/agent_provider_interface.rs |   5 ++
 tests/terminal_app.rs             |  33 +++++--
 tests/workspace.rs                |  54 +++++++++---
 8 files changed, 293 insertions(+), 66 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index 1c5bdc9..48eba11 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -163,6 +163,9 @@ rather than using `@work-leaf` read, patch, or lock directives.
 
 - `AgentBackend::launch` starts an agent session from an `AgentLaunch`.
 - `AgentBackend::send` sends a prompt to an existing agent session.
+- `AgentBackend::command` runs a raw slash-prefixed backend command against an existing agent
+  session. Providers that do not support backend commands return the default unsupported-command
+  reply instead of sending the text through the normal prompt path.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming` and `AgentBackend::send_streaming` provide real-time output to a
   sink of `AgentStreamEvent` values. Their default implementations call the non-streaming methods.
 - `AgentBackend::launch_streaming_interruptible` and
@@ -187,10 +190,11 @@ then kill to remaining registered processes. This behavior is used by provider i
 spawn real processes.
 
 New agent providers implement `AgentBackend`; they do not add provider logic to `src/codex.rs`.
-Providers that need real-time UI output should override the streaming methods. Providers implemented
-inside this crate can use the crate-private process registration helpers for shared shutdown.
-Providers outside this crate can implement launch, send, and streaming through the public trait; a
-public lifecycle extension is required before external child processes can participate in the shared
+Providers that support slash commands override `command`, and providers that need real-time UI
+output should override the streaming methods. Providers implemented inside this crate can use the
+crate-private process registration helpers for shared shutdown. Providers outside this crate can
+implement launch, send, command handling, and streaming through the public trait; a public lifecycle
+extension is required before external child processes can participate in the shared
 `AgentShutdownHandle` registry.
 
